1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,000
All right!

2
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Yes!

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:21,000
Someone needs to fill in for Yoshitsune.

4
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Akutsu, you're playing forward.

5
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Great!

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
The center-back's playing as a forward now?

7
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
He's not freakin' Tulio!

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:33,000
Being promoted doesn't necessarily mean you're ready for a match.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:36,000
If you're not getting much game time on the A-team,

10
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
I'll try to field you in the B-team games,

11
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
so make sure you're leaving those times available.

12
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Feels like we're not really on the team, just in limbo.

13
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:48,000
If they want me to earn my place, then so be it.

14
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,000
Give me one month.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
I'll be the best starter they've ever seen.

16
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:54,000
Hmm. Oh, well. I guess I can't expect too much.

17
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,000
I am surprised Ashito wasn't promoted, though.

18
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
We won both games thanks to him, so I figured he'd be a lock.

19
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Yeah.

20
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Hmm.

21
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
I thought they'd be moving him up despite his problem areas.

22
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:08,000
I mean, we all have them.

23
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,000
It's Fukuda, right?

24
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
He's known to make bold choices when it comes to his players.

25
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Hey. Where is he?

26
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,000
Uh-huh.

27
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Huh.

28
00:02:48,042 --> 00:03:00,902
Aisaku Otomo, Soichiro Tachibana, Ashito Aoi.

29
00:03:01,802 --> 00:03:03,822
Those are my picks for this year's tryouts.

30
00:03:03,922 --> 00:03:05,282
They're the only ones worth remembering.

31
00:03:06,122 --> 00:03:07,222
Aoi won't cut it.

32
00:03:07,702 --> 00:03:09,782
No amount of practice will get him where we need him.

33
00:03:10,442 --> 00:03:13,722
He's never gonna have what it takes to play on Aspirion's front line.

34
00:03:14,322 --> 00:03:16,302
I'm gonna turn him into a defender.

35
00:03:19,042 --> 00:03:19,982
What you think?

36
00:03:20,402 --> 00:03:22,242
Wait, you mean as a fullback?

37
00:03:22,782 --> 00:03:25,062
That's right. It makes sense to me.

38
00:03:26,162 --> 00:03:28,722
No way. He won't want to change his position.

39
00:03:29,142 --> 00:03:30,522
We can't just force him to.

40
00:03:31,062 --> 00:03:33,102
I need your support. Trust me.

41
00:03:34,042 --> 00:03:36,702
I'll be the one to tell him when the time's right.

42
00:03:48,042 --> 00:03:54,522
Whoa. Hold on. Does Ashito know about this yet?

43
00:03:54,882 --> 00:03:56,362
They're trying to make him a defender?

44
00:03:56,822 --> 00:03:59,162
The dude self-destructs if he's not allowed to score.

45
00:04:01,682 --> 00:04:03,942
Later. I'm going for a jog.

46
00:04:04,222 --> 00:04:04,642
What?

47
00:04:04,642 --> 00:04:07,662
Yeah, I'm out.

48
00:04:07,762 --> 00:04:08,742
We need to find him.

49
00:04:09,462 --> 00:04:11,142
Oh, okay. I get it.

50
00:04:11,282 --> 00:04:13,082
The idiot doesn't have a cell phone, does he?

51
00:04:13,242 --> 00:04:14,042
Wait for me!

52
00:04:15,842 --> 00:04:18,622
Um, you know, it is almost curfew.

53
00:04:19,142 --> 00:04:21,022
So I guess I should really get going, too.

54
00:04:21,022 --> 00:04:44,842
Today's the enrollment ceremony.

55
00:04:45,302 --> 00:04:46,262
Is this a joke?

56
00:04:46,462 --> 00:04:47,902
You're fielding Aoi as a forward?

57
00:04:47,902 --> 00:04:51,002
Just when are you planning to tell him about the Switch?

58
00:04:51,722 --> 00:04:54,682
It's just for a couple of games. Not that big a deal.

59
00:04:55,102 --> 00:04:57,602
What exactly is the point of that?

60
00:04:58,342 --> 00:05:02,122
Before we can discuss his position, he needs to master the basics.

61
00:05:02,822 --> 00:05:04,342
Let him play what he knows.

62
00:05:05,162 --> 00:05:07,042
His skills have got to improve first.

63
00:05:08,422 --> 00:05:10,002
I've said this before.

64
00:05:10,862 --> 00:05:12,562
He's not going to accept it.

65
00:05:13,322 --> 00:05:15,722
You can't make him do anything he doesn't want.

66
00:05:17,902 --> 00:05:26,802
Listen. He's by the window now.

67
00:05:27,382 --> 00:05:28,682
I want you to motivate him.

68
00:05:29,322 --> 00:05:32,542
Say he don't think he'll cut it as a forward loud enough for him to hear.

69
00:05:33,442 --> 00:05:35,222
His strength lies in his defiance.

70
00:05:36,362 --> 00:05:39,042
I promise this is the best thing we can do for him.

71
00:05:39,042 --> 00:05:41,142
But I need you to be the bad guy.

72
00:05:41,702 --> 00:05:42,342
I'm sorry.

73
00:05:43,022 --> 00:05:43,542
Please.

74
00:05:44,622 --> 00:05:45,182
Fukuda.

75
00:05:46,102 --> 00:05:49,062
Up to now, everything's turned out the way you said it would.

76
00:05:49,862 --> 00:05:52,342
Things always happen the way you predict they will.

77
00:05:52,842 --> 00:05:54,102
It's an unspoken rule.

78
00:05:54,662 --> 00:05:55,562
We all know it.

79
00:05:55,562 --> 00:06:08,282
I can't believe we killed it.

80
00:06:08,462 --> 00:06:10,282
That means I really am good enough, Nozomi.

81
00:06:10,662 --> 00:06:11,242
It's true.

82
00:06:11,742 --> 00:06:13,462
No one would have guessed this was your debut.

83
00:06:14,462 --> 00:06:15,542
Give me three years.

84
00:06:16,582 --> 00:06:18,502
I'll be a key player by then.

85
00:06:19,182 --> 00:06:22,582
I'll make a name for myself out here and then head off to Europe.

86
00:06:23,462 --> 00:06:24,502
It's going to happen.

87
00:06:24,982 --> 00:06:25,802
Just watch me.

88
00:06:27,402 --> 00:06:29,182
You're a piece of work, Fukuda.

89
00:06:29,822 --> 00:06:30,502
This plan?

90
00:06:31,162 --> 00:06:32,842
Ashito Aoi playing fullback?

91
00:06:32,842 --> 00:06:41,062
If by some miracle he agrees to it, that'll open up unlimited possibilities for both of you.

92
00:06:41,642 --> 00:06:47,042
However, I can't allow you to bulldoze your way through this time.

93
00:06:47,902 --> 00:06:50,082
Was this really the best way to go about it?

94
00:06:50,902 --> 00:06:52,502
Was it the appropriate moment?

95
00:06:52,962 --> 00:06:54,622
Or did you finally get it wrong?

96
00:06:56,582 --> 00:06:57,382
We'll see.

97
00:06:58,522 --> 00:07:00,762
I just got a strange text from Yuma.

98
00:07:00,762 --> 00:07:03,762
He said Aoi hasn't been back to the dorm at all.

99
00:07:04,242 --> 00:07:05,362
Have you heard from him, Hana?

100
00:07:05,902 --> 00:07:07,742
Do you have any idea where he might be?

101
00:07:30,762 --> 00:07:45,942
Look at me.

102
00:07:45,942 --> 00:07:45,962
Look at me.

103
00:08:00,762 --> 00:08:02,902
There's no life in your eyes.

104
00:08:05,662 --> 00:08:06,702
Have you eaten yet?

105
00:08:10,322 --> 00:08:11,222
All clear.

106
00:08:11,982 --> 00:08:12,802
Perfect, right?

107
00:08:13,262 --> 00:08:14,662
Place is completely vacant.

108
00:08:15,042 --> 00:08:16,802
No one from the academy is using it today.

109
00:08:17,502 --> 00:08:19,642
I knew they wouldn't be because I used to work here.

110
00:08:20,162 --> 00:08:20,982
You can sit wherever.

111
00:08:21,402 --> 00:08:22,342
I'm going to cook for you.

112
00:08:22,342 --> 00:08:35,902
Boom, now what?

113
00:08:37,182 --> 00:08:37,582
Hana.

114
00:08:37,822 --> 00:08:38,002
Hmm?

115
00:08:38,622 --> 00:08:40,862
You showed up like you knew where I would be.

116
00:08:41,302 --> 00:08:42,262
But how could you?

117
00:08:42,942 --> 00:08:46,862
Henri told me what happened earlier, and then I just sort of filled in the gaps.

118
00:08:47,622 --> 00:08:50,142
Match had finished a while ago, but you weren't at the dorm.

119
00:08:50,142 --> 00:08:56,462
Oh, you were still on your kit, so in a crowd, you'd be spotted and someone would let the team know right away.

120
00:08:57,342 --> 00:09:01,022
Which meant you couldn't be downtown or at the train station.

121
00:09:02,282 --> 00:09:06,262
I may not know much about soccer, but even I could figure out this would be tough on you.

122
00:09:07,222 --> 00:09:12,662
I knew you would be taking it hard and that you'd want to run, maybe even as far as home to Ehime.

123
00:09:12,662 --> 00:09:16,382
In order to get there, you'd have to go to a bus stop first.

124
00:09:17,902 --> 00:09:22,542
Still, I didn't really think I'd find you, but I sure did.

125
00:09:22,722 --> 00:09:23,342
First try.

126
00:09:23,602 --> 00:09:25,462
Like, there, you were.

127
00:09:25,462 --> 00:09:38,562
I think I completely blacked out until you showed up.

128
00:09:39,242 --> 00:09:41,882
Even sitting at this table feels like we're in a dream.

129
00:09:42,982 --> 00:09:44,162
Here's what I do know.

130
00:09:44,902 --> 00:09:46,082
Your brother's a jerk.

131
00:09:47,762 --> 00:09:48,722
He's a monster.

132
00:09:48,722 --> 00:09:55,042
I'm sure it feels that way, but he has a reason for everything.

133
00:09:57,462 --> 00:10:05,442
Regardless, I don't know what it means to change positions, but I know being the one to score was truly important to you.

134
00:10:06,522 --> 00:10:07,282
I'm sorry.

135
00:10:10,322 --> 00:10:11,542
So what will you do?

136
00:10:11,542 --> 00:10:16,202
Are you gonna quit?

137
00:10:19,082 --> 00:10:20,382
I won't quit.

138
00:10:21,562 --> 00:10:23,162
Couldn't afford to anyway.

139
00:10:23,662 --> 00:10:24,482
I'm stuck here.

140
00:10:29,882 --> 00:10:33,162
I'll zone out a bit longer, then I'll head back.

141
00:10:33,822 --> 00:10:34,582
I've got to.

142
00:10:35,542 --> 00:10:36,522
I'm sorry, Hana.

143
00:10:36,962 --> 00:10:38,122
It all looks good.

144
00:10:38,122 --> 00:10:41,502
But the last thing on my mind is eating.

145
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:49,242
I'm a defender.

146
00:10:51,222 --> 00:10:51,782
Defender?

147
00:10:52,462 --> 00:10:52,982
How?

148
00:11:01,702 --> 00:11:03,122
What's going on?

149
00:11:04,422 --> 00:11:04,902
Hello?

150
00:11:05,762 --> 00:11:06,742
Hana, it's late.

151
00:11:06,742 --> 00:11:08,162
Why are you calling at this hour?

152
00:11:10,302 --> 00:11:11,142
Are you there?

153
00:11:11,582 --> 00:11:12,682
Is everything okay?

154
00:11:13,882 --> 00:11:14,282
Hello?

155
00:11:20,862 --> 00:11:21,262
Ashito.

156
00:11:23,902 --> 00:11:25,402
Ashito, is that you?

157
00:11:25,822 --> 00:11:26,782
It is, right?

158
00:11:27,142 --> 00:11:28,142
Did something happen?

159
00:11:28,142 --> 00:11:28,202
Did something happen?

160
00:11:28,202 --> 00:11:42,902
Don't get too worked up, okay?

161
00:11:46,402 --> 00:11:49,362
If it's not panning out, then just come home.

162
00:11:49,722 --> 00:11:51,282
I promise, it's not a big deal.

163
00:11:51,282 --> 00:12:01,022
Nothing's changed.

164
00:12:01,462 --> 00:12:02,042
I'm fine.

165
00:12:03,322 --> 00:12:04,282
Everything's great.

166
00:12:04,662 --> 00:12:05,322
I promise.

167
00:12:06,322 --> 00:12:07,222
Please don't worry.

168
00:12:08,842 --> 00:12:09,362
Night.

169
00:12:09,362 --> 00:12:09,402
Night.

170
00:12:09,402 --> 00:12:22,782
I know it's a lot of pressure and probably really overwhelming, but don't tell yourself

171
00:12:22,782 --> 00:12:23,982
you only have one option.

172
00:12:24,662 --> 00:12:28,902
Don't sit there with that look in your eyes and say you can't afford to quit.

173
00:12:29,342 --> 00:12:34,622
Like I said, I don't know much about this sport, so I don't know what you're going through.

174
00:12:34,622 --> 00:12:41,682
But I'm hoping you'll take a step back and see it's just soccer, for goodness sake.

175
00:12:44,142 --> 00:12:45,782
I heard your mom on the phone.

176
00:12:46,142 --> 00:12:47,182
She was being supportive.

177
00:12:47,622 --> 00:12:49,002
She's there, whatever you decide.

178
00:12:54,582 --> 00:12:55,842
I'm hungry now.

179
00:12:56,182 --> 00:12:56,642
Can I?

180
00:12:58,522 --> 00:12:59,282
Of course.

181
00:12:59,282 --> 00:12:59,362
Yes.

182
00:12:59,362 --> 00:13:25,642
Hey, Akutsu.

183
00:13:25,642 --> 00:13:27,442
I heard a bunch of chaos in the lobby.

184
00:13:27,442 --> 00:13:28,622
Did something happen?

185
00:13:29,362 --> 00:13:31,122
Oh, Kuromayashi?

186
00:13:32,802 --> 00:13:34,202
What are you doing here?

187
00:13:34,602 --> 00:13:36,762
Since when do you dwell amongst the lowly?

188
00:13:37,402 --> 00:13:39,442
Aren't you on the bench for J1's game tomorrow?

189
00:13:42,122 --> 00:13:45,142
There was someone here I was hoping to chat with before the match.

190
00:13:45,722 --> 00:13:47,122
You've seen Ashito Aoi?

191
00:13:49,422 --> 00:13:52,122
Anyway, it's not that important.

192
00:13:53,082 --> 00:13:54,082
I just can't find him.

193
00:13:55,222 --> 00:13:58,422
The chaos you heard in the lobby before was about him.

194
00:13:58,422 --> 00:14:00,382
He hasn't returned to the dorm yet.

195
00:14:01,422 --> 00:14:02,122
How come?

196
00:14:02,822 --> 00:14:06,022
He was useless as a forward, so he got switched to a defender.

197
00:14:06,422 --> 00:14:08,542
Then he stormed off, pouting like a loser.

198
00:14:09,902 --> 00:14:12,362
I hope that dude quits and doesn't come back.

199
00:14:12,922 --> 00:14:15,082
But why would he quit over something like that, huh?

200
00:14:15,262 --> 00:14:17,062
He should totally play fullback on the line.

201
00:14:17,562 --> 00:14:18,782
It's clear if you watch him.

202
00:14:19,342 --> 00:14:20,662
He wouldn't have gotten in otherwise.

203
00:14:20,662 --> 00:14:22,942
You knew that, right?

204
00:14:25,042 --> 00:14:27,702
Hey, you know, you should coach him on how to defend.

205
00:14:28,442 --> 00:14:30,322
I mean, that would make the most sense, don't you think?

206
00:14:30,422 --> 00:14:31,162
Shut up!

207
00:14:32,562 --> 00:14:34,662
Come on, we used to talk about this a lot.

208
00:14:35,562 --> 00:14:39,302
About how we needed a fullback to complete Fukuda's big picture.

209
00:14:39,302 --> 00:14:40,302
Ashito!

210
00:14:41,102 --> 00:14:42,522
Where the heck have you been?

211
00:14:44,622 --> 00:14:46,282
We looked everywhere for you.

212
00:14:46,362 --> 00:14:46,962
Where'd you go?

213
00:14:47,042 --> 00:14:47,522
You did?

214
00:14:47,702 --> 00:14:48,802
Oh, I'm sorry, man.

215
00:14:49,382 --> 00:14:49,962
Mm-hmm.

216
00:14:50,542 --> 00:14:51,722
So what the crap?

217
00:14:56,302 --> 00:14:56,782
Curfew.

218
00:14:57,002 --> 00:14:57,742
I broke it.

219
00:14:58,262 --> 00:15:00,142
Gotta go apologize to the dorm, Mom.

220
00:15:01,262 --> 00:15:01,742
Ashito.

221
00:15:01,742 --> 00:15:01,862
Hmm.

222
00:15:01,862 --> 00:15:01,902
Hmm.

223
00:15:01,902 --> 00:15:03,862
Hmm.

224
00:15:03,862 --> 00:15:03,982
Hmm.

225
00:15:03,982 --> 00:15:04,022
Hmm.

226
00:15:04,022 --> 00:15:04,262
Hmm.

227
00:15:08,262 --> 00:15:08,942
Hmm.

228
00:15:08,942 --> 00:15:21,942
You gotta be kidding me right now.

229
00:15:22,622 --> 00:15:24,802
You're completely useless as a forward,

230
00:15:24,942 --> 00:15:27,162
so we're supposed to train you as a defender instead?

231
00:15:27,862 --> 00:15:29,622
Do you know how big of a pain in the ass

232
00:15:29,622 --> 00:15:31,542
that's gonna be for the rest of us defenders?

233
00:15:34,042 --> 00:15:35,702
Did that hit a nerve?

234
00:15:36,442 --> 00:15:38,922
You know, maybe soccer's not for you.

235
00:15:38,942 --> 00:15:40,442
Are you ready to give up?

236
00:15:52,622 --> 00:15:53,142
Hmm.

237
00:15:54,622 --> 00:15:55,942
I am not giving up.

238
00:15:55,942 --> 00:15:58,182
But I don't know how to defend.

239
00:15:59,242 --> 00:16:01,102
So I'm going to need your help.

240
00:16:01,482 --> 00:16:03,082
Please teach me everything you know.

241
00:16:03,622 --> 00:16:03,822
Huh?

242
00:16:08,402 --> 00:16:10,642
Thank you for this, Hana.

243
00:16:12,222 --> 00:16:14,062
I don't want to be a defender.

244
00:16:14,522 --> 00:16:15,662
I really don't.

245
00:16:16,302 --> 00:16:19,362
But there's no other way.

246
00:16:19,362 --> 00:16:20,162
I don't want to be a defender.

247
00:16:20,162 --> 00:16:20,362
Hmm?

248
00:16:22,362 --> 00:16:22,722
Hmm.

249
00:16:23,722 --> 00:16:25,622
He seems to have a lot going on.

250
00:16:26,282 --> 00:16:27,382
I can try him another time.

251
00:16:28,822 --> 00:16:31,442
I'm curious about this meal plan I found last week.

252
00:16:32,262 --> 00:16:33,662
I wonder who made it for him.

253
00:16:34,322 --> 00:16:36,202
The more I look at it, the better it seems.

254
00:16:36,202 --> 00:16:46,542
What happened to your face, bro?

255
00:16:47,082 --> 00:16:49,042
The doorm mother sent me flying.

256
00:16:49,662 --> 00:16:52,562
She is seriously scary when you piss her off.

257
00:16:52,822 --> 00:16:54,502
Well, you ready?

258
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:55,322
Maybe.

259
00:16:55,882 --> 00:16:56,522
For what?

260
00:16:56,802 --> 00:16:59,242
We're going to go over the basics of being a defender.

261
00:16:59,962 --> 00:17:02,322
I hope you didn't think anyone else was going to teach you.

262
00:17:02,322 --> 00:17:08,142
Mind if I join you, too?

263
00:17:08,642 --> 00:17:10,002
I figure I owe you one.

264
00:17:10,582 --> 00:17:11,622
Uh, hey, Asuri.

265
00:17:11,962 --> 00:17:12,842
You owe me?

266
00:17:13,262 --> 00:17:15,022
You mean because of that fight?

267
00:17:15,382 --> 00:17:17,722
I'm a cut above, so I'm moving up to the A-team.

268
00:17:18,162 --> 00:17:19,042
As a parting gift,

269
00:17:19,422 --> 00:17:21,642
I thought I'd teach you a little bit about being a defender.

270
00:17:22,542 --> 00:17:24,342
Look, I'm not Kodura or Takashima,

271
00:17:24,802 --> 00:17:26,222
so I can be here, right?

272
00:17:28,442 --> 00:17:29,302
Um, hello?

273
00:17:29,302 --> 00:17:36,942
Thank you, both of you.

274
00:17:38,202 --> 00:17:39,762
I would love your help!

275
00:17:41,762 --> 00:17:43,322
So, you're a defender now.

276
00:17:43,742 --> 00:17:45,742
That's going to change up the game a lot for you.

277
00:17:45,922 --> 00:17:46,982
It won't be easy.

278
00:17:47,742 --> 00:17:49,522
In fact, one thing in particular

279
00:17:49,522 --> 00:17:51,482
I know you'll struggle with.

280
00:17:52,122 --> 00:17:52,482
Uh-huh.

281
00:17:53,102 --> 00:17:54,342
Well, am I right?

282
00:17:55,302 --> 00:17:56,182
The shuffle.

283
00:17:56,182 --> 00:17:59,882
I suggest you figure out the full meaning of that word.

284
00:18:00,622 --> 00:18:01,842
If you can't do that,

285
00:18:01,922 --> 00:18:03,642
then you won't be playing a single game.

286
00:18:03,842 --> 00:18:04,242
Feel me?

287
00:18:04,922 --> 00:18:05,562
Uh...

288
00:18:05,562 --> 00:18:11,322
So, about the shuffle.

289
00:18:11,842 --> 00:18:12,542
Let me see.

290
00:18:12,782 --> 00:18:15,162
I guess we can say we start off with four defenders.

291
00:18:15,662 --> 00:18:17,882
Then one of the fullbacks starts heading upfield.

292
00:18:18,742 --> 00:18:19,802
Once they leave,

293
00:18:19,862 --> 00:18:22,222
that's going to create a big old space right here.

294
00:18:23,222 --> 00:18:25,722
It's up to you to fill that space quickly.

295
00:18:27,622 --> 00:18:29,282
So, how would you do that?

296
00:18:32,422 --> 00:18:34,962
Look at your other defenders.

297
00:18:35,462 --> 00:18:37,782
You'll see all three of them start shuffling sideways.

298
00:18:38,922 --> 00:18:40,342
They're keeping it tight in the center.

299
00:18:41,082 --> 00:18:43,022
Moving over to plug a huge gap like that

300
00:18:43,022 --> 00:18:44,182
is what we call the shuffle.

301
00:18:44,722 --> 00:18:45,242
Got it?

302
00:18:45,582 --> 00:18:47,002
Makes it harder to reach the goal.

303
00:18:47,062 --> 00:18:47,402
Hey!

304
00:18:47,562 --> 00:18:48,702
I was going to say that!

305
00:18:48,822 --> 00:18:49,182
No.

306
00:18:49,182 --> 00:18:51,642
Oh, this is ridiculous.

307
00:18:54,582 --> 00:18:56,662
Even I can tell you that much?

308
00:18:56,762 --> 00:18:57,622
Come on!

309
00:19:01,302 --> 00:19:02,522
Fukuda's not here.

310
00:19:02,902 --> 00:19:04,542
We'll train as a group first,

311
00:19:04,722 --> 00:19:06,522
then we can play a quick mini-game

312
00:19:06,522 --> 00:19:07,702
and call it for the day.

313
00:19:08,742 --> 00:19:10,822
A and B teams will split into two groups,

314
00:19:11,022 --> 00:19:11,682
nine each.

315
00:19:11,682 --> 00:19:14,442
Then do 20-minute nine-on-nines.

316
00:19:15,102 --> 00:19:16,722
The goal for this exercise

317
00:19:16,722 --> 00:19:18,862
is to make sure each member of your team

318
00:19:18,862 --> 00:19:21,962
has a clear idea of their position and its role.

319
00:19:22,662 --> 00:19:24,602
Therefore, I suggest you refrain

320
00:19:24,602 --> 00:19:26,082
from getting overly physical.

321
00:19:26,842 --> 00:19:27,242
All right.

322
00:19:27,522 --> 00:19:28,962
Take a second to check the lineups

323
00:19:28,962 --> 00:19:30,162
and confirm your positions.

324
00:19:34,642 --> 00:19:35,202
So,

325
00:19:35,562 --> 00:19:37,442
old man Fukuda dipped out.

326
00:19:38,042 --> 00:19:38,682
It's fine.

327
00:19:38,682 --> 00:19:40,742
Actually, I'm glad he's not here.

328
00:19:41,282 --> 00:19:42,482
I don't want to see him.

329
00:19:43,702 --> 00:19:44,582
I'll do it.

330
00:19:45,422 --> 00:19:46,682
I'll give this a try.

331
00:19:46,682 --> 00:20:03,602
Looks like Asari and Kuda

332
00:20:03,602 --> 00:20:04,882
are having a tough time.

333
00:20:05,742 --> 00:20:06,182
Man,

334
00:20:06,322 --> 00:20:07,942
that A-team's not messing around.

335
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:09,382
Am I right, Ashito?

336
00:20:09,382 --> 00:20:09,502
Oh,

337
00:20:09,502 --> 00:20:15,602
come on, hurry it up.

338
00:20:15,602 --> 00:20:17,682
Unless you're not wanting to play today.

339
00:20:17,902 --> 00:20:18,362
I do!

340
00:20:30,362 --> 00:20:31,482
How are you feeling?

341
00:20:33,242 --> 00:20:34,462
Not too bad.

342
00:20:36,162 --> 00:20:37,222
That's good to hear.

343
00:20:37,642 --> 00:20:38,662
Just do your best.

344
00:20:38,662 --> 00:20:48,482
Seriously?

345
00:20:48,482 --> 00:21:07,242
A fullback stands this far away from everything?

346
00:21:07,242 --> 00:21:09,622
It's a totally different view from a forwards.

347
00:21:10,242 --> 00:21:12,082
It's like a whole new perspective.

348
00:21:12,622 --> 00:21:14,162
I can see everyone from here.

349
00:21:14,602 --> 00:21:15,182
My team,

350
00:21:15,442 --> 00:21:16,022
their team.

351
00:21:16,402 --> 00:21:18,842
I can keep an eye on every player as a fullback.

352
00:21:19,222 --> 00:21:20,282
It's an advantage.

353
00:21:20,682 --> 00:21:21,622
It's good you're here.

354
00:21:23,502 --> 00:21:23,982
Listen,

355
00:21:24,342 --> 00:21:25,322
just do your best.

356
00:21:25,662 --> 00:21:26,742
I control the line.

357
00:21:27,022 --> 00:21:28,062
All eyes on me.

358
00:21:28,062 --> 00:21:32,402
Both Togashi and I

359
00:21:32,402 --> 00:21:34,002
were full attack-minded.

360
00:21:35,002 --> 00:21:36,342
If you want advice on defending,

361
00:21:37,182 --> 00:21:38,762
then Takashima is your best bet.

362
00:21:40,822 --> 00:21:42,842
Aspirion's a major attacking team now,

363
00:21:43,062 --> 00:21:45,062
but he's been a defender since he was a kid.

364
00:21:45,842 --> 00:21:47,322
The attack against Sekio worked

365
00:21:47,322 --> 00:21:49,662
because we knew Takashima had our backs.

366
00:21:50,442 --> 00:21:51,462
Um, actually,

367
00:21:51,462 --> 00:21:54,422
I was wondering if there was anything

368
00:21:54,422 --> 00:21:55,722
I should do specifically.

369
00:22:00,962 --> 00:22:01,882
The shuffle.

370
00:22:02,502 --> 00:22:04,802
Since that's the whole point of being a fullback.

371
00:22:07,102 --> 00:22:09,182
If you can manage to get that down,

372
00:22:09,702 --> 00:22:11,782
then I don't care if you go and join the attack

373
00:22:11,782 --> 00:22:12,802
or stay out here.

374
00:22:12,802 --> 00:22:20,862
I've made up my mind.

375
00:22:21,742 --> 00:22:23,422
I'm ready to crush this.

376
00:22:24,282 --> 00:22:25,362
Let's go!

377
00:22:33,362 --> 00:22:33,922
Hmm.

378
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,686
Next time on Awashi, where I ought to be.

